IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1965 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 5 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 1 other than the definitions table: s 2(1) chapeau and rules of reading,
-- s 2(2), (2A), (3), the deleted subsections, and s 2A (criteria for determining death).
-- (s 2(5), deemed service by post, is in sgia-interpretation-time.l4 with the other time rules.)
-- Policy for "unless the contrary intention appears" / "unless the context otherwise requires":
-- a rule under that phrase takes a plain yes/no input and answers NOTHING when it is TRUE (NOTES.md finding 2).

§ `Section 2(1) -- to what the definitions apply`

-- src:166 | 2.—(1) In this Act, and in every written law enacted before, on or
-- src:167 | after 28 December 1965 (but without affecting anything done before
-- src:168 | that date) —
@ref s 2(1) chapeau (src:166-168)
GIVEN `the day a written law was enacted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the definitions in section 2(1) apply to a written law enacted on` `the day a written law was enacted` MEANS
    -- "before, on or after 28 December 1965": every date
    TRUE

@ref s 2(1) chapeau, without affecting anything done before 28 December 1965 (src:167-168)
GIVEN `the day a thing was done` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the definitions in section 2(1) affect a thing done on` `the day a thing was done` MEANS
    `the day a thing was done` AT LEAST Date 28 12 1965

§ `Section 2(1) -- the rules of reading (the masculine, the singular and the plural)`

-- Who a word is applied to. The Act says "females"; it says nothing about words importing the feminine.
DECLARE `Gender of the person the word is applied to` IS ONE OF
    Male
    Female

DECLARE `Number of a word` IS ONE OF
    Singular
    Plural

-- src:554 | words importing the masculine gender include females;
@ref s 2(1) words importing the masculine gender (src:554-554)
GIVEN `the person the word is applied to` IS A `Gender of the person the word is applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 2(1) extends a word importing the masculine gender to` `the person the word is applied to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person the word is applied to`
    WHEN Female THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN Male THEN NOTHING

-- Words importing the feminine gender: the Act says nothing, in either direction.
GIVEN `the person the word is applied to` IS A `Gender of the person the word is applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 2(1) extends a word importing the feminine gender to` `the person the word is applied to` MEANS NOTHING

-- src:556 | words in the singular include the plural and words in the plural
-- src:557 | include the singular;
@ref s 2(1) words in the singular include the plural and the plural the singular (src:556-557)
GIVEN `the number of the word` IS A `Number of a word`
      `the number of what is meant` IS A `Number of a word`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 2(1) extends a word in one number to what is meant in the other` `the number of the word` `the number of what is meant` MEANS
    IF `the number of the word` EQUALS `the number of what is meant`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 2(2) and (2A) -- other forms of a defined word; a definition a written law provides`

-- The three limbs of s 2(2): other parts of speech, other grammatical forms, cognate expressions.
DECLARE `Variant of a defined word` IS ONE OF
    `another part of speech`
    `another grammatical form`
    `a cognate expression`

-- src:586 | (2) Where a word or expression is defined in a written law, then,
-- src:587 | unless the contrary intention appears, other parts of speech and
-- src:588 | grammatical forms of that word or expression, and cognate
-- src:589 | expressions, have corresponding meanings in that law.
@ref s 2(2) (src:586-589)
GIVEN `the variant` IS A `Variant of a defined word`
      `the word is defined in the written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a variant of a defined word has a corresponding meaning in that law` `the variant` `the word is defined in the written law` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the word is defined in the written law` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN CONSIDER `the variant`
         WHEN `another part of speech` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `another grammatical form` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a cognate expression` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:591 | (2A) If a written law provides for a definition to apply, the
-- src:592 | definition applies unless the context otherwise requires.
@ref s 2(2A) (src:591-592)
GIVEN `a written law provides for a definition to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the definition a written law provides applies` `a written law provides for a definition to apply` `the context otherwise requires` MEANS
    IF `a written law provides for a definition to apply`
    THEN JUST (NOT `the context otherwise requires`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 2(3) -- references in a written law enacted before 28 December 1965`

-- One row of s 2(3): the old expressions, what each is to be construed as, and the two qualifications the
-- Act attaches to some rows ("unless the context otherwise requires", "as the case may require").
-- Where the Act pairs its old expressions with its new ones ("respectively", s 2(3)(l)), each old expression has
-- its own replacement; `construed as` keeps the words exactly as the Act prints them.
DECLARE `Paired replacement` HAS
    `old expression` IS A STRING
    `new expression` IS A STRING

DECLARE `Old reference` HAS
    paragraph IS A STRING
    `old expressions` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `construed as` IS A STRING
    `unless the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as the case may require` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each construed as` IS A LIST OF `Paired replacement`

-- src:601 | (a) references to the Colony of the Straits Settlements, the
-- src:602 | Settlement of Singapore, the Colony of Singapore, the
-- src:603 | Colony, the State of Singapore or the State, are to be
-- src:604 | construed as references to Singapore;
@ref s 2(3)(a) (src:601-604)
`s 2(3)(a)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(a)", (LIST "the Colony of the Straits Settlements", "the Settlement of Singapore", "the Colony of Singapore", "the Colony", "the State of Singapore", "the State"), "Singapore", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY

-- src:606 | (b) references to the Federated Malay States are, unless the
-- src:607 | context otherwise requires, to be construed as references to
-- src:608 | the States of Malaya;
@ref s 2(3)(b) (src:606-608)
`s 2(3)(b)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(b)", (LIST "the Federated Malay States"), "the States of Malaya", TRUE, FALSE, EMPTY

-- src:610 | (c) references to the Governor of the Malayan Union are to be
-- src:611 | construed as references to the Yang di‑Pertuan Agong;
@ref s 2(3)(c) (src:610-611)
`s 2(3)(c)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(c)", (LIST "the Governor of the Malayan Union"), "the Yang di-Pertuan Agong", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY

-- src:613 | (d) references to the Malayan Union are to be construed as
-- src:614 | references to Malaysia or the territories comprised therein,
-- src:615 | as the case may require;
@ref s 2(3)(d) (src:613-615)
`s 2(3)(d)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(d)", (LIST "the Malayan Union"), "Malaysia or the territories comprised therein", FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY

-- src:617 | (e) references to the Chief Justice or to any court, judge or
-- src:618 | magistrate of the Malayan Union or of the Federated Malay
-- src:619 | States or of any of the Malay States are to be construed as
-- src:620 | references to the Chief Justice or to the corresponding
-- src:621 | court, judge or magistrate of Malaysia or the territories
-- src:622 | comprised therein, as the case may require;
@ref s 2(3)(e) (src:617-622)
`s 2(3)(e)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(e)", (LIST "the Chief Justice", "any court of the Malayan Union", "any judge of the Malayan Union", "any magistrate of the Malayan Union", "any court of the Federated Malay States", "any judge of the Federated Malay States", "any magistrate of the Federated Malay States", "any court of any of the Malay States", "any judge of any of the Malay States", "any magistrate of any of the Malay States"), "the Chief Justice or the corresponding court, judge or magistrate of Malaysia or the territories comprised therein", FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY

-- src:624 | (f) references to any officer of, or authority or body
-- src:625 | constituted in or for, the Federated Malay States, any
-- src:626 | Malay State or the Malayan Union are to be construed as
-- src:627 | references to the corresponding officer of, or authority or
-- src:628 | body constituted in or for, Malaysia or the territories
-- src:629 | comprised therein, as the case may require;
@ref s 2(3)(f) (src:624-629)
`s 2(3)(f)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(f)", (LIST "an officer of the Federated Malay States", "an authority or body constituted in or for the Federated Malay States", "an officer of any Malay State", "an authority or body constituted in or for any Malay State", "an officer of the Malayan Union", "an authority or body constituted in or for the Malayan Union"), "the corresponding officer of, or authority or body constituted in or for, Malaysia or the territories comprised therein", FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY

-- src:631 | (g) references to the Assembly or the Legislative Assembly
-- src:632 | are to be construed as references to the Parliament;
@ref s 2(3)(g) (src:631-632)
`s 2(3)(g)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(g)", (LIST "the Assembly", "the Legislative Assembly"), "the Parliament", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY

-- src:634 | (h) references to the Yang di-Pertuan Negara are to be
-- src:635 | construed as references to the President;
@ref s 2(3)(h) (src:634-635)
`s 2(3)(h)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(h)", (LIST "the Yang di-Pertuan Negara"), "the President", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY

-- src:637 | (i) references to the Federal Minister are to be construed as
-- src:638 | references to the appropriate Minister of Singapore;
@ref s 2(3)(i) (src:637-638)
`s 2(3)(i)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(i)", (LIST "the Federal Minister"), "the appropriate Minister of Singapore", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY

-- src:640 | (j) references to the State Advocate‑General are to be
-- src:641 | construed as references to the Attorney‑General;
@ref s 2(3)(j) (src:640-641)
`s 2(3)(j)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(j)", (LIST "the State Advocate-General"), "the Attorney-General", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY

-- src:646 | (k) references to the High Court in Singapore are to be
-- src:647 | construed as references to the High Court of Singapore;
-- src:648 | and
@ref s 2(3)(k) (src:646-648)
`s 2(3)(k)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(k)", (LIST "the High Court in Singapore"), "the High Court of Singapore", FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY

-- src:650 | (l) references to a Judge of the High Court and the Registrar of
-- src:651 | the High Court are to be construed as references to a Judge
-- src:652 | of the Supreme Court and the Registrar of the Supreme
-- src:653 | Court, respectively.
@ref s 2(3)(l) (src:650-653)
`s 2(3)(l)` MEANS
    `Old reference` OF "(l)", (LIST "a Judge of the High Court", "the Registrar of the High Court"), "a Judge of the Supreme Court and the Registrar of the Supreme Court, respectively", FALSE, FALSE, LIST (`Paired replacement` OF "a Judge of the High Court", "a Judge of the Supreme Court"), (`Paired replacement` OF "the Registrar of the High Court", "the Registrar of the Supreme Court")

-- src:599 | (3) In every written law enacted before 28 December 1965 —
@ref s 2(3) chapeau (src:599-599)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Old reference`
`the twelve rows of section 2(3)` MEANS
    LIST `s 2(3)(a)`, `s 2(3)(b)`, `s 2(3)(c)`, `s 2(3)(d)`, `s 2(3)(e)`, `s 2(3)(f)`, `s 2(3)(g)`, `s 2(3)(h)`, `s 2(3)(i)`, `s 2(3)(j)`, `s 2(3)(k)`, `s 2(3)(l)`

@ref s 2(3) chapeau, every written law enacted before 28 December 1965 (src:599-599)
GIVEN `the old expression` IS A STRING
      `the day the written law was enacted` IS A DATE
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`a reference in an old written law is to be construed as` `the old expression` `the day the written law was enacted` `the context otherwise requires` MEANS
    IF `the day the written law was enacted` AT LEAST Date 28 12 1965
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER filter (GIVEN row YIELD elem `the old expression` (row's `old expressions`)) `the twelve rows of section 2(3)`
         WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
         WHEN row FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
             IF row's `unless the context otherwise requires` AND `the context otherwise requires`
             THEN NOTHING
             ELSE CONSIDER filter (GIVEN pair YIELD pair's `old expression` EQUALS `the old expression`) (row's `each construed as`)
                  WHEN pair FOLLOWED BY more THEN JUST (pair's `new expression`)
                  WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST (row's `construed as`)

-- The words the Act prints for an old expression, whole, as the Act has them (for (l): both replacements and "respectively").
-- It does not ask the day or the context: it is the text of the row, not the answer for a given law.
-- src:599 | (3) In every written law enacted before 28 December 1965 —
@ref s 2(3) the words the Act prints for each old expression (src:599-599)
GIVEN `the old expression` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the words section 2(3) prints for` `the old expression` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN row YIELD elem `the old expression` (row's `old expressions`)) `the twelve rows of section 2(3)`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN row FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (row's `construed as`)

§ `Section 2(4) and (6) -- deleted`

-- src:655 | (4) [Deleted by Act 5 of 2014]
@ref s 2(4) deleted (src:655-655)
`s 2(4) is deleted` MEANS "(4) [Deleted by Act 5 of 2014]"

-- src:665 | (6) [Deleted by Act 5 of 2025 wef 09/03/2025]
@ref s 2(6) deleted (src:665-665)
`s 2(6) is deleted` MEANS "(6) [Deleted by Act 5 of 2025 wef 09/03/2025]"

§ `Section 2A -- criteria for determining death`

-- src:669 | 2A.—(1) For all purposes, a person has died when there has
-- src:670 | occurred either —
-- src:672 | (a) irreversible cessation of circulation of blood and
-- src:673 | respiration in the body of the person; or
-- src:675 | (b) total and irreversible cessation of all functions of the brain
-- src:676 | of the person.
@ref s 2A(1) (src:669-676)
GIVEN `circulation of blood and respiration have irreversibly ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all functions of the brain have totally and irreversibly ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person has died` `circulation of blood and respiration have irreversibly ceased` `all functions of the brain have totally and irreversibly ceased` MEANS
    `circulation of blood and respiration have irreversibly ceased`
    OR `all functions of the brain have totally and irreversibly ceased`

-- Which ground the death is determined on, and whether an organ is to be removed after death under the
-- Human Organ Transplant Act 1987 or the Medical (Therapy, Education and Research) Act 1972.
DECLARE `Ground of death` IS ONE OF
    `irreversible cessation of circulation of blood and respiration`
    `total and irreversible cessation of all functions of the brain`

-- What a determination of death must satisfy. The numbers and yes/no fields are what the Act requires.
DECLARE `What the determination requires` HAS
    `ordinary standards of current medical practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prescribed criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
    `medical practitioners who must certify` IS A NUMBER
    `at least one not involved in the care or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `none involved in the care or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `none in the team that will remove the organ` IS A BOOLEAN
    `none involved in selecting the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
    `none to be involved in the recipient's care in hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prescribed postgraduate medical qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:678 | (2) The determination of the irreversible cessation of circulation of
-- src:679 | blood and respiration in the body of a person must, subject to
-- src:680 | subsection (5), be made in accordance with the ordinary standards of
-- src:681 | current medical practice.
-- src:683 | (3) The determination of the total and irreversible cessation of all
-- src:684 | functions of the brain of a person must, subject to subsections (4) and
-- src:685 | (6), be made in accordance with the prescribed criteria.
-- src:687 | (4) Except in the circumstances referred to in subsection (6), the
-- src:688 | determination of the total and irreversible cessation of all functions of
-- src:693 | the brain of a person must be certified in the prescribed form by
-- src:694 | 2 medical practitioners —
-- src:696 | (a) at least one of whom has not been involved in the care or
-- src:697 | treatment of the person so certified; and
-- src:699 | (b) who possess the prescribed postgraduate medical
-- src:700 | qualifications.
-- src:702 | (5) If the death of a person from whose body an organ is to be
-- src:703 | removed after his or her death as authorised under the Human Organ
-- src:704 | Transplant Act 1987 or the Medical (Therapy, Education and
-- src:705 | Research) Act 1972 is determined by the irreversible cessation of
-- src:706 | circulation of blood and respiration in the body of that person, the
-- src:707 | person’s death must be certified in the prescribed form by 2 medical
-- src:708 | practitioners —
-- src:710 | (a) who have not been involved in the care or treatment of the
-- src:711 | person so certified;
-- src:713 | (b) who do not belong to the team of medical practitioners that
-- src:714 | will effect the removal of the organ from the body;
-- src:716 | (c) who have not been involved in the selection of the
-- src:717 | proposed recipient of the organ; and
-- src:719 | (d) who will not be involved in the care or treatment of the
-- src:720 | proposed recipient of the organ during his or her
-- src:721 | hospitalisation for the purpose of the transplant.
-- src:723 | (6) If the death of a person from whose body an organ is to be
-- src:724 | removed after his or her death as authorised under the Human Organ
-- src:725 | Transplant Act 1987 or the Medical (Therapy, Education and
-- src:726 | Research) Act 1972 is determined by the total and irreversible
-- src:727 | cessation of all functions of the brain of that person, the person’s
-- src:728 | death must be certified in the prescribed form by 2 medical
-- src:729 | practitioners —
-- src:731 | (a) who have not been involved in the care or treatment of the
-- src:732 | person so certified;
-- src:734 | (b) who do not belong to the team of medical practitioners that
-- src:735 | will effect the removal of the organ from the body;
-- src:740 | (c) who have not been involved in the selection of the
-- src:741 | proposed recipient of the organ;
-- src:743 | (d) who will not be involved in the care or treatment of the
-- src:744 | proposed recipient of the organ during his or her
-- src:745 | hospitalisation for the purpose of the transplant; and
-- src:747 | (e) who possess the prescribed postgraduate medical
-- src:748 | qualifications.
@ref s 2A(2) to (6) what a determination must satisfy (src:678-748)
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Ground of death`
      `an organ is to be removed after death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What the determination requires`
`what the determination of death requires` `the ground` `an organ is to be removed after death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `irreversible cessation of circulation of blood and respiration` THEN
        -- (2): ordinary standards of current medical practice, subject to (5)
        IF `an organ is to be removed after death`
        THEN `What the determination requires` OF TRUE, FALSE, 2, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
        ELSE `What the determination requires` OF TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
    WHEN `total and irreversible cessation of all functions of the brain` THEN
        -- (3): the prescribed criteria; (4): certified by 2 practitioners, one not involved in the care, qualified;
        -- (6) replaces (4) when an organ is to be removed: all (a) to (d) and the qualifications (e)
        IF `an organ is to be removed after death`
        THEN `What the determination requires` OF FALSE, TRUE, 2, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
        ELSE `What the determination requires` OF FALSE, TRUE, 2, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

@ref s 2A(4) the certificate and its signatories (src:687-700)
GIVEN `medical practitioners who certified` IS A NUMBER
      `at least one has not been involved in the care or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they possess the prescribed postgraduate medical qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `certified in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certificate meets section 2A(4)` `medical practitioners who certified` `at least one has not been involved in the care or treatment` `they possess the prescribed postgraduate medical qualifications` `certified in the prescribed form` MEANS
    `medical practitioners who certified` AT LEAST 2
    AND `at least one has not been involved in the care or treatment`
    AND `they possess the prescribed postgraduate medical qualifications`
    AND `certified in the prescribed form`

@ref s 2A(5) organ removal, circulatory ground (src:702-721)
GIVEN `medical practitioners who certified` IS A NUMBER
      `none has been involved in the care or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `none belongs to the team that will remove the organ` IS A BOOLEAN
      `none has been involved in selecting the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `none will be involved in the recipient's care in hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `certified in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certificate meets section 2A(5)` `medical practitioners who certified` `none has been involved in the care or treatment` `none belongs to the team that will remove the organ` `none has been involved in selecting the recipient` `none will be involved in the recipient's care in hospital` `certified in the prescribed form` MEANS
    `medical practitioners who certified` AT LEAST 2
    AND `none has been involved in the care or treatment`
    AND `none belongs to the team that will remove the organ`
    AND `none has been involved in selecting the recipient`
    AND `none will be involved in the recipient's care in hospital`
    AND `certified in the prescribed form`

@ref s 2A(6) organ removal, brain ground (src:723-748)
GIVEN `medical practitioners who certified` IS A NUMBER
      `none has been involved in the care or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `none belongs to the team that will remove the organ` IS A BOOLEAN
      `none has been involved in selecting the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `none will be involved in the recipient's care in hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they possess the prescribed postgraduate medical qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `certified in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certificate meets section 2A(6)` `medical practitioners who certified` `none has been involved in the care or treatment` `none belongs to the team that will remove the organ` `none has been involved in selecting the recipient` `none will be involved in the recipient's care in hospital` `they possess the prescribed postgraduate medical qualifications` `certified in the prescribed form` MEANS
    `medical practitioners who certified` AT LEAST 2
    AND `none has been involved in the care or treatment`
    AND `none belongs to the team that will remove the organ`
    AND `none has been involved in selecting the recipient`
    AND `none will be involved in the recipient's care in hospital`
    AND `they possess the prescribed postgraduate medical qualifications`
    AND `certified in the prescribed form`

-- src:761 | (8) Nothing in this section —
-- src:763 | (a) affects the operation of section 110 of the Evidence
-- src:764 | Act 1893 (burden of proving that a person is alive who has
-- src:765 | not been heard of for 7 years), section 100 of the Women’s
-- src:766 | Charter 1961 (proceedings for interim judgment of
-- src:767 | presumption of death and divorce) or any other written
-- src:768 | law relating to the presumption of death;
@ref s 2A(8)(a) (src:761-768)
GIVEN `a written law relates to the presumption of death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 2A affects the operation of a written law on the presumption of death` `a written law relates to the presumption of death` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:770 | (b) prevents the certification or determination of death in a
-- src:771 | case where the body of a person is not found or recovered.
-- src:773 | [42/2005]
@ref s 2A(8)(b) (src:770-773)
GIVEN `the body of the person is not found or recovered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 2A prevents the certification or determination of death` `the body of the person is not found or recovered` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:775 | (9) In this section, “medical practitioner” means a person who is
-- src:776 | registered, or deemed to be registered, as a medical practitioner under
-- src:777 | the Medical Registration Act 1997.
@ref s 2A(9) (src:775-777)
GIVEN `registered as a medical practitioner under the Medical Registration Act 1997` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deemed to be registered as a medical practitioner under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a medical practitioner for section 2A` `registered as a medical practitioner under the Medical Registration Act 1997` `deemed to be registered as a medical practitioner under that Act` MEANS
    `registered as a medical practitioner under the Medical Registration Act 1997`
    OR `deemed to be registered as a medical practitioner under that Act`
